<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Active primary progressive multiple sclerosis (G35.B1)</content>. Stable, with no infection; ready for ocrelizumab after today&apos;s vaccines. [S]<list><item>Recombinant zoster dose 2 and hepatitis B dose 2 today.</item><item>First ocrelizumab half-dose in two weeks and the second two weeks later, on days without teaching, with premedication and at least one hour of observation.</item><item>Infusion center to confirm no active infection before each dose.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Spastic gait and fall risk (R26.89)</content>. Baclofen tolerated with less stiffness and no added weakness. The physical therapy evaluation is overdue. [S]<list><item>Increase baclofen to 10 mg three times a day.</item><item>Clinic to ask the physical therapy service today for the first available date, with a second provider if none is offered within three weeks.</item><item>Daily stretching and her home exercises meanwhile.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Neurogenic bladder (N31.9)</content>. Better on mirabegron; blood pressure unchanged. [S]<list><item>Continue mirabegron 25 mg daily.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Examination</td><td>New or worsening symptoms (relapse, pseudo-relapse with heat or infection)</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No new symptoms</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Disability: EDSS and timed 25-foot walk</td><td>Every visit, and at least every 6 months</td><td>Up to date</td><td>EDSS 6.0 five weeks ago; gait unchanged today</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Brain MRI</td><td>At diagnosis with gadolinium; re-baseline 3 to 6 months after starting therapy; then yearly without routine gadolinium</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Diagnostic MRI five weeks ago; re-baseline due three to six months after the first dose</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccines before therapy (PCV20, recombinant zoster x2, Tdap, hepatitis B x2)</td><td>Inactivated at least 2 weeks and live at least 4 weeks before the first dose</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Zoster dose 2 and hepatitis B dose 2 today; series complete; first infusion two weeks from today</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Infusion reactions and infections</td><td>Each infusion, and every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No infection today; premedication and observation planned</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spasticity (modified Ashworth) and baclofen tolerance</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Modified Ashworth 1+; baclofen increased to 10 mg three times a day</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Bladder: urgency, nocturia, urinary infection, and blood pressure on mirabegron</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Nocturia once; blood pressure 120/76 on mirabegron</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Falls, walking aids and physical therapy</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: the physical therapy evaluation requested at intake has not happened because of a waiting list. No harm so far: no falls and her gait is unchanged. Corrective action: the clinic asked the service today for the first available date, with a second provider if none is offered within three weeks; daily stretching and home exercises meanwhile</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Workplace accommodation</td><td>At intake and with any change</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Accommodations agreed by her employer</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Diagnosis confirmed and classified, vaccines completed at least two weeks before therapy, and a disease-modifying therapy started within ten weeks. In progress; target 1980-06-29 [S]</item><item>No falls through eight months. In progress; target 1980-10-26 [S]</item><item>25-hydroxyvitamin D at least 30 ng/mL within four months. In progress; target 1980-06-29 [S]</item><item>Up no more than once a night to pass urine within three months. In progress; target 1980-06-29 [S]</item><item>Keep her full teaching and speaking schedule with the accommodations she chooses. In progress; target 1980-10-26 [S]</item><item>No new or enlarging T2 lesions on the re-baseline MRI. In progress; target 1980-10-26 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis B vaccine (HepB-CpG), dose 2 of 2; Recombinant zoster vaccine, dose 2 of 2 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Practice guideline recommendations summary: Disease-modifying therapies for adults with multiple sclerosis (Rae-Grant A, et al.; PMID 29686116) (2018); 2021 MAGNIMS-CMSC-NAIMS consensus recommendations on the use of MRI in patients with multiple sclerosis (Wattjes MP, et al.; PMID 34139157) (2021); Practice guideline update summary: Vaccine-preventable infections and immunization in multiple sclerosis (Farez MF, et al.; PMID 31462584) (2019); OCREVUS (ocrelizumab) injection, prescribing information (2026); Multiple sclerosis in adults: management (NG220) (2022); Accommodation and Compliance: Multiple Sclerosis (2026); Introduction to the Americans with Disabilities Act (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, osteoporosis and depression monographs (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Ocrelizumab infusions in two and four weeks at the infusion center. Review six weeks after the second infusion with a blood count, CD19 count, vitamin D and the PHQ-9. Next scheduled visit 1980-06-29: four-month review, six weeks after the first ocrelizumab doses: infusion tolerance, infections, blood counts, vitamin D, heat and mood. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
